# Keep the build context (and image) lean. The Dockerfile only needs the Python
# workspace + scripts; everything below is irrelevant or large.

# Large local data dumps — the v1 archive export (~92 MB) is loaded into Postgres
# by the archive-load Job from Spaces, NOT baked into the image.
data/

# Python
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
.venv/
**/.venv/
.pytest_cache/
**/.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/*.egg-info/
dist/
build/

# Node deps + the marketing site aren't needed by the build. The web UI (web/) IS
# built by the Dockerfile's web-builder stage and baked into the runtime image via
# `COPY --from=web-builder /app/web/dist`, so web/ and the pnpm workspace manifests
# (package.json / pnpm-workspace.yaml / pnpm-lock.yaml) + the TS contracts package
# MUST stay in the build context. The final image stays lean because only web/dist
# is copied into the runtime stage. node_modules is reinstalled fresh by pnpm.
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
web/dist/
site/
**/.vite/
coverage/

# Local SQLite system-of-record + WAL (dev only).
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal

# Infra / deploy / CI / docs / VCS — not needed at run time.
infra/
.github/
docs/
history/
.git/
.gitignore
.mcp.json

# Env / secrets — never copy into an image.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/
.gstack/
.claude/
